virtio_p9fs: finalize feature negotiation

vt9p_attach() negotiated features but, unlike every other virtio driver,
never called virtio_finalize_features(), so FEATURES_OK was never set.
Legacy devices do not care, but modern (virtio 1.0) devices may refuse to
process requests until it is; with Sedna's, the first request (Tversion)
is never answered and mounting times out after 120 seconds.

diff --git a/sys/dev/virtio/p9fs/virtio_p9fs.c b/sys/dev/virtio/p9fs/virtio_p9fs.c
index 2b276a60aa9a..b9689ba319fa 100644
--- a/sys/dev/virtio/p9fs/virtio_p9fs.c
+++ b/sys/dev/virtio/p9fs/virtio_p9fs.c
@@ -324,6 +324,11 @@ vt9p_attach(device_t dev)
 	/* Negotiate the features from the host */
 	virtio_set_feature_desc(dev, virtio_9p_feature_desc);
 	virtio_negotiate_features(dev, VIRTIO_9PNET_F_MOUNT_TAG);
+	error = virtio_finalize_features(dev);
+	if (error != 0) {
+		device_printf(dev, "cannot finalize features\n");
+		goto out;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * If mount tag feature is supported read the mount tag
